Reject oversized numeric subscripts before converting them to R_xlen_t.

In realSubscript(), an out-of-range double can become an invalid R_xlen_t
when used as the requested length of a growable vector. A later assignment
then writes beyond the allocation in EnlargeVector(). The four-statement
reproducer for OSS-Fuzz testcase 6491489048526848 uses x[1e19] <- 0.

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R), not
carried here.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #415, filed 2026-10-28.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

--- a/src/main/subscript.c
+++ b/src/main/subscript.c
@@ -807,7 +807,11 @@ realSubscript(SEXP s, R_xlen_t ns, R_xlen_t nx, R_xlen_t *stretch,
 	} else isna = true;
     }
     if (max >= (double)nx+1.) {
-#ifndef LONG_VECTOR_SUPPORT
+#ifdef LONG_VECTOR_SUPPORT
+	/* Avoid an out-of-range conversion to R_xlen_t. */
+	if (max > R_XLEN_T_MAX)
+	    ECALL(call, _("subscript too large"));
+#else
 	if (max > INT_MAX) {
 	    ECALL(call, _("subscript too large for 32-bit R"));
 	}
